RITISH HOME-GPU LICENSE v1.1

Copyright (c) 2026 Rambarun Komaljeet

PURPOSE

This research exists so that people can train and run language models on
hardware they already own — a laptop, a gaming GPU, a single consumer card.
It is deliberately available to those people, including for work that earns
them a living. It is deliberately NOT available to the organisations whose
scale this work exists as an alternative to.

DEFINITIONS

"Software" means the source code, documentation, data, and research
materials in this repository.

"Large Entity" means any organisation, or any group of affiliated
organisations under common control, that meets ANY of the following:

  (a) is primarily engaged in developing, training, hosting, or selling
      foundation models or large language models — including but not
      limited to OpenAI, Anthropic, Google/DeepMind, Meta, Microsoft,
      Amazon, Apple, xAI, Mistral, Cohere, DeepSeek, Alibaba, ByteDance,
      Baidu, Tencent, and NVIDIA;

  (b) has more than 100 employees or contractors;

  (c) has annual gross revenue exceeding USD 5,000,000;

  (d) has raised more than USD 5,000,000 in cumulative equity or
      debt financing;

  (e) operates, rents, or has access to more than 64 datacentre-class
      GPU accelerators (A100/H100-class or equivalent) for the purposes
      of the use in question.

"Permitted User" means anyone who is not a Large Entity, and who is not
acting for, on behalf of, or at the direction of a Large Entity. This
expressly includes individuals in salaried employment, freelancers, small
studios and startups below the thresholds above, students, hobbyists,
educators, non-profits, and academic researchers.

PERMISSIONS

A Permitted User is granted the right to:

  - View, copy, modify, and distribute the Software
  - Use the Software for personal, educational, research, hobby, and
    commercial purposes, including in paid work and in products or
    services that generate revenue

provided that ALL conditions below are met.

Employment by a Large Entity does not by itself disqualify you. Using the
Software for that employer's benefit does.

CONDITIONS

1. NO LARGE-ENTITY USE — A Large Entity may not use, run, train with,
   evaluate with, incorporate, or distribute the Software or any
   derivative of it, for any purpose, including internal research and
   evaluation. If you are unsure whether an entity qualifies, contact
   the author.

2. NO TRAINING-DATA USE — The Software, and any text or code derived
   from this repository, may not be used as training data, fine-tuning
   data, evaluation data, or benchmark material for any model produced
   by or for a Large Entity.

3. ATTRIBUTION — Any use or distribution must retain this license and
   clearly credit: Rambarun Komaljeet —
   https://gitlab.com/komalbarun/kramba-ai

4. SHARE-ALIKE — Any modified version must be distributed under this
   same license, with these restrictions intact.

5. NO SUBLICENSING — You may not grant others rights beyond what this
   license permits, and you may not relicense the Software or a
   derivative in a way that would make it available to a Large Entity.

LICENSING FOR LARGE ENTITIES

A Large Entity wishing to use this Software must obtain a separate
written license from the author:

  komalbarun@gmail.com

